{%- comment -%}
  Amplitude Browser SDK in the MAIN page context.

  The Shopify "Amplitude" app web pixel runs sandboxed (STRICT runtime, no DOM), so it
  cannot power heatmaps or expose window.amplitude to the theme. Loading the Browser SDK
  here does three things the sandboxed pixel can't:
    1. autocapture.elementInteractions -> feeds Amplitude Heatmaps / element clicks.
    2. activates the theme's existing window.amplitude.track() calls (Web_Shopify_*),
       which were dormant no-ops without a main-context SDK.
    3. getDeviceId() works, so the checkout stitch (stampCart writes _amp_device_id to the
       cart -> order.note_attributes) can attach the server-side "Checkout Completed" event
       (fired by the ops-tool order webhook) to this exact shopper.
  API key is the public client key (safe in client JS), same project as the app pixel.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
(function () {
  if (window.amplitude && window.amplitude._iq) return; /* already loaded */
  var s = document.createElement('script');
  s.async = true;
  s.src = 'https://cdn.amplitude.com/libs/analytics-browser-2.11.11-min.js.gz';
  s.onload = function () {
    try {
      window.amplitude.init('955e3f5f6695674ba9db9bd3a94857ad', {
        serverZone: 'US',
        /* elementInteractions is OFF by default -> turn it on for heatmaps; the other
           autocapture channels (pageViews, sessions, formInteractions, attribution)
           keep their default (on). */
        autocapture: { elementInteractions: true }
      });
    } catch (e) {}
  };
  (document.head || document.documentElement).appendChild(s);
})();
</script>
